===============================================================================
BIOMEDICAL RESEARCH & CLINICAL INVESTIGATIONAL USE DISCLAIMER
(WHO Class II Software as a Medical Device - SaMD Guidelines)
===============================================================================
EchoSpiro is an experimental research prototype engineered for the VITB - Johns
Hopkins University Health-Hack 2027 under IRB Protocol JHU-IRB-2027-0184. 
It demonstrates active contactless ultrasonic Doppler continuous-wave (CW) 
demodulation in edge browser environments.

This software has NOT received 510(k) clearance or PMA approval from the United
States Food and Drug Administration (FDA), European CE-Mark Certification, or
equivalent national medical regulatory authorisations for primary diagnostic use. 

This platform is intended exclusively for investigational clinical research,
triage benchmarking, educational simulation, and humanitarian edge prototyping.
It must NOT be used as the sole basis for clinical diagnosis, critical emergency
decisions, or therapeutic prescription without secondary validation by a licensed
pulmonologist or certified gold-standard pneumotachographic spirometry.
